commit 5fc4d77a1b8bdc2d8a34ff1f1e48f94e118da05c
Author:     Brendan Abolivier <brendan@thunderbird.net>
AuthorDate: Mon Mar 9 12:11:57 2026 +0200
Commit:     Brendan Abolivier <brendan@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Mon Mar 9 12:11:57 2026 +0200

    Bug 2011672 - Support POST requests and alternative bodies for Graph. r=jtracey


    This patch does a bit more than just support POST requests for Graph.

    POST support is implemented by essentially generalising the existing support for
    PATCH requests from bug 2013310, and making `graph_xpcom` use the method from
    the `http::Request` when setting the method on the `moz_http` side (I've also
    taken the opportunity to make `moz_http` use the `http::Method` enum rather than
    its own, now we're already using the `http` crate for other things).

    I've also added support for alternative request bodies. `POST /me/messages` and
    `POST /me/sendMail` both support sending messages as a base64-encoded RFC822
    blob with the `text/plain` content type, which isn't represented in the OpenAPI
    spec. This allows consumers to deviate from the OpenAPI spec whenever desired by
    providing the body bytes and content type themselves.

    I've also included some drive-by improvements we discussed, such as changing the
    receiver for `build`/`build_request` from `&self` to `self`, which avoids
    cloning request bodies, and I've renamed `Operation::build` into
    `Operation::build_request` which is imo a bit clearer. I'm happy to revert the
    latter renaming, if it's a bit too disruptive or not desired.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D286212

